&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll thrive as a Senior Marketing Manager, Web Growth if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think in systems, not campaigns.&lt;/strong&gt; When a channel underperforms, you look at the signal layer, not the campaign copy. When a page converts, you ask what feedback loop just closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship and iterate.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather run ten disciplined tests than debate one perfect page. You have a bias toward getting a valid experiment live this week, and a hypothesis-first instinct for what to test next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are technically fluent enough to be dangerous.&lt;/strong&gt; You can read a Marketo trigger, sanity-check a schema markup change, QA a page built in Webflow, and interpret a Tableau attribution model without a translator. You partner with GTM Engineering as a peer, not a customer.&lt;/li&gt;
